2.2.0 - 9/24/2026
- Remove branch from prebuilt targets remote path
- Quote the arguments the target dispatcher forwards
- Keep an argument holding a space in one piece for target test and dist
- Remove deprecated buildbox_get_prebuilt utility

2.1.4 - 9/15/2026
- Add '-u' option to 'project clone' and '-a' to 'project update'
- Abort package update if remote repository history changed
- Keep packages source sharing aligned with config
- Fix packages sources sharing when no build mode is defined

2.1.3 - 9/11/2026
- Add clone, build, test and dist project commands, to address all targets at once
- Doc: BuildBox SBOM tools to generate the Software Bill of Materials (CRA compliance)
- Doc: add cheat sheet
- Restart the project container when its directory has been replaced, a re-clone at the same path leaving the old one mounted

2.1.2 - 9/8/2026
- Target package update feature
- Fix missing target fastbuild command
- Ensure container hostname do not exceed HOST_NAME_MAX
- Avoid accumulating target variables

2.1.1 - 9/3/2026
- Improved target variables evaluation
- Tools packages now support revision including '/'
- Reviewed shell completions
- Improve locks API mechanisms
- Claude skills

2.1.0 - 8/31/2026
- System, user, and project level config files
- Compilation settings are now read from the target file only
- Locks are now released when the process holding them is gone
- Avoid masking builtin 'set' with conflicting target function
- Export API wrappers

2.0.2 - 6/2/2026
- Shell plugin: add project name in prompt
- Improved tables columns display
- Resolve 'goto <pkg>' stdout conflicts
- If project profile is an empty Git repo (no commits yet), read branch from symbolic ref

2.0.1 - 5/6/2026
- Fix host commands pipes and output file paths
- Handle direct calls and nested 'bash -c' calls for BuildBox API
- Allocate a TTY only when stdin is a terminal for container shell
- Fix custom registry image pull
